# cr-hello: the C++ half of milestone CR-a (docs/CR-PLAN.md, track CT1):
# a C++ program built by Jam OS's clang toolchain (tools/jamos-clang++,
# LLVM's runtimes from ports/llvm-runtimes) that runs from /data:
# exceptions thrown across files and through destructors, static
# constructors, eight threads with thread_local, a guarded static,
# std::atomic's wait (a futex), iostreams, std::filesystem on /data. Its
# output is the same on any C++ system: files/expected.txt, which
# tools/cr-test.sh checks against the build host's own build of it and
# the test (`test`) against the Jam OS run. Jam OS's own code (`local`).
name        cr-hello
version     1
revision    1
summary     a C++ test program for Jam OS's clang toolchain (CR-a)
category    tests
licence     BSD-2-Clause
licence-file LICENSE
local       files
place       package
style       custom
toolchain   clang
needs       llvm-runtimes
# It writes its scratch directory in /data (wants/cr-hello).
program     bin/cr-hello
files       share/cr-hello/expected.txt
